      "extract": "Denote by Km the m-twist knot (m ≥0) in S3, by EKm its exterior (i.e. the complement in S3 of a regular neighborhood). Bullock and Lofaro have proved the following result. Theorem 1 (Bullock, Lofaro [BL]). The Kauﬀman bracket skein module of the complement of a regular neighborhood of the m-twist knot is the free C[t, t−1]-module with basis xiyj, i ≥0, 0 ≤j ≤m, where x and y are the curves described in Figure 2. m 2",
